    In that collider component, check Is Trigger ✅ — this lets the master overlap it without physically bumping into it

    A.1.3.b Make sure the master can detect triggers
    Trigger events need a Rigidbody2D on at least one of the two colliding objects. Since the node is static, put it on the master:
    Click on master in the Hierarchy
    Add Component → Rigidbody2D
    Set Body Type to Kinematic (you're moving it via transform.position, not physics forces, 
    so you don't want gravity/physics pushing it around)
    Add Component → box Collider 2D (leave "Is Trigger" unchecked on this one — one trigger + one normal collider in the pair is enough)

    A.1.3.c Write the ResourceNode script
    This lives on the node itself and knows what it gives and how it depletes/respawns.
    Create Scripts/ResourceNode.cs

        using UnityEngine;
        
        public class ResourceNode : MonoBehaviour
        {
            public string resourceName = "Stick";
            public int amount = 1;
            public float respawnTime = 10f;
        
            private SpriteRenderer sr;
            private Collider2D col;
            private bool isDepleted = false;
        
            void Awake()
            {
                sr = GetComponent<SpriteRenderer>();
                col = GetComponent<Collider2D>();
            }
        
            public void Gather()
            {
                if (isDepleted) return;
        
                GuildMaster.Instance.AddResource(resourceName, amount);
                Deplete();
            }
        
            void Deplete()
            {
                isDepleted = true;
                sr.enabled = false;
                col.enabled = false;
                Invoke(nameof(Respawn), respawnTime);
            }
        
            void Respawn()
            {
                isDepleted = false;
                sr.enabled = true;
                col.enabled = true;
            }
        }

    Attach this to StickNode in the Inspector (Add Component → Resource Node). You'll see Resource Name, Amount, Respawn Time fields 
    — leave defaults or set Amount to 1, Respawn Time to 10.

